../../guards/jev-prewave.md:10:Judge whether this build record shows a recreation ready to be scored, or one whose defects are already visible in its own paperwork. Price: (1) PARAMETERIZATION — is the piece genuinely CONFIG-driven (fields named, ranges sane), or hard-coded with a config costume? (2) PURITY PRE-CHECK — does the construction route describe generation from parameters, with no tracing/embedding step hiding in the prose? (3) OWN-CHECKS COMPLETENESS — are the mechanical guards' results recorded (purity grep, swap test, syntax), or asserted? **Census-checkpoint mapping (Amendment A11, landed 2026-11-17, Cycle 028 Condense): every Observe census checkpoint for the item must map to an executable own-check assertion whose evaluation instant is CONFIG-derived; the build-record identifies checkpoint · assertion · CONFIG expression · evaluated result. ASSERTED-CHECKS is returned if any checkpoint lacks this mapping, any evaluation instant uses hardcoded defaults, or execution evidence is absent; a CONFIG timing swap must be shown to move the corresponding assertion's evaluation instant. Receipt form (Amendment A12, landed 2026-11-18, Cycle 035 Condense): the execution evidence for each assertion is its EXECUTABLE RECEIPT — harness command or run · CONFIG expression evaluated · raw result from the build under review (for a timing swap, the receipt shows the changed evaluation instant); a claim without its receipt is execution evidence absent. **Receipt-index ground (Amendment A13, landed 2026-11-18, Cycle 036 Condense): a build-record whose RECEIPT INDEX (INSTRUCTION A13.1) is missing an expected entry (an applicable guards.md command, a planned A11 assertion, an assertion inherited whole from a prior attempt's filed harness, or a census row for an expected CONFIG key), carries an exclusion whose disposition cites no governing plan or guard, or carries a populated receipt lacking the evidence its assertion requires (CONFIG expression + evaluated value for CONFIG-derived inputs; raw observed result for checks) is an ASSERTED-CHECKS ground by name.** The same leg prices the A6 fit evidence: a fit-table row lacking measurement provenance, or carrying model-derived bounds, per guard-measured-fit.md checks 1–2 is an ASSERTED-CHECKS ground.** (4) TECHNIQUE FIDELITY PLAN — does the record state which packet mechanics the build implements and which it deliberately defers (a deferral named is lawful; a mechanic silently absent is not)? Score 0–1 per dimension, classify defects. You judge paperwork only: a build can pass you and still fail its wave — your job is that no wave is spent on a build its own record already condemns.
../../guards/jev-prewave.md:25:- Any dimension < 0.5 → HOLD · ASSERTED-CHECKS at any score on other dimensions → HOLD (unrecorded checks are the lane's named failure class).
../../guards/jev-observe-exit.md:27:- Dimensions (0–1): queue-state-priced · prior-scores-read · mechanics-seen · variables-extracted · guidance-carried · consumer-named. (1.0 = evidenced in the record with citations; 0.5 = asserted without citation; 0.0 = absent.)
../../guards/jev-observe-exit.md:28:- Rejection taxonomy (one primary per returned item): QUEUE-STALE (queue position/status not read this cycle) · REATTEMPT-MISROUTED (scored technique in a first-attempt wave) · SCORES-UNREAD (prior scores/cures exist, uncited) · MECHANICS-UNSEEN (no firsthand sub-beat record) · VARIABLES-THIN (variable list cannot bind a parameter table) · GUIDANCE-DROPPED (standing family guidance absent from working memory) · CONSUMER-VAGUE.
../../guards/jev-observe-exit.md:32:- Any dimension < 0.5 → RETURN-TO-OBSERVE for that item. GUIDANCE-DROPPED on a particle-field or typography item → RETURN-TO-OBSERVE at any other score (T15 attempt 1's founding lesson: the frozen-flow defect and both owner catches were guidance-shaped failures discovered only after the wave was spent).
