294:3. **Parameterization — the table and swaps leave the known failure paths open.** §P1 lacks explicit bindings or derivations for per-column entrance and count-up anchors, placeholder form and reveal mode, ratio-label placement and arrow curvature, person-glyph visibility, and column placement and vertical rhythm. It also names both `cascadeMs` and a fixed `dotStaggerMs` without assigning ownership of completion. With 36 dots, a 28 ms stagger and 220 ms settle put the last completion at `35 × 28 + 220 = 1,200 ms` after the first start. As specified, changing `cascadeMs` alone gives no guarantee that this span changes. Make `cascadeMs` the authoritative window, derive stagger after accounting for settle, and give single-dot reveals an explicit rule. Bind or derive the missing values in CONFIG and list their application sites. Extend the swap to exercise one and three columns and assert event order, generated marks, ratios, and layout. Replace the CP1–CP7 specimen indices and quantities with assertions against configured event roles and values. At CP3, assert the column-wise reveal pattern as well as the count. (T208 §§O3, P1, P3–P5; T53 `scores.md`, cure 1; T82 `scores.md`, cure 1; T45 `scores.md`, cures 1, 2, and 5.)
